# Files

# Wildcard files.
*.a
*.o
*.dll
*.exe
*.bak
*.ini
test*
# ...but not the conformance suite. `test*` was written to catch stray scratch
# binaries and it swallowed test/ whole: the suite built and passed here and
# would never have been committed. The directory has to be un-ignored before
# anything inside it can be, because git does not descend into an excluded
# directory. Build output still lands in dist/, which stays ignored.
!test/
!test/*/
!test/*.h
!test/*.cpp
!test/fixtures/*.c
!test/fixtures/*.rc
!test/fixtures/*.json
# zlib only. It is prebuilt and carried as-is: pure C with no thread-model
# dependency, so one archive links under any toolchain. leveldb is deliberately
# NOT un-ignored - it is compiled from libraries/leveldb/src/ by `make libs`,
# because a prebuilt C++ archive silently encodes the thread model it was built
# with and then links under only half of them.
!libraries/leveldb/lib/libz.a

# Folders
.vscode/
dist/
pack/
.VSCodeCounter/
.idea/
packaging/
